## andrej-karpathy-skills

https://github.com/multica-ai/andrej-karpathy-skills, cloned at `2c60614`.

    MIT, stated in the repository README. Copyright: multica-ai, the owner of
    that repository, for the compilation. The underlying guidelines are Andrej
    Karpathy's public statements.

The repository ships no `LICENSE` file and GitHub reports no licence for it
(checked again on 2026-08-19: `license: null`, and `contents/LICENSE` is a 404),
so this notice records the grant as the README makes it rather than reproducing
a file that does not exist. A licence stated plainly in a README is a grant by
the repository owner; it is weaker as evidence than a licence file, and that is
why the exact wording is written out here.

**Nothing of their expression is distributed any more.** On 2026-08-18 the
eight-word method reported `core/PRINCIPLES.md` **P2** as 55% shared with the
source — a genuine copy — and **P3** as clean. Measuring again on 2026-08-19 at
four window sizes showed the second number to be an artefact of the window: P3
shared its heading and opening sentence word for word, and P1 and P7, never
measured at all, carried runs of nine and ten words. All four were rewritten
that day. `bin/primeskills-shingle` now reports the longest run shared with this
donor as four words, and that run is a section heading.

The debt that remains is to the ideas, which are named in `ATTRIBUTIONS.md` and
here. The grant above is recorded because it covered what we shipped before the
rewrite, and because the notice costs nothing to keep.

